scripts/dream.sh now reports what each dream run spent, and it's committed as 05317a97. The tests pass, but nothing has run in production yet: the next dream run is at least 7 days away, so it's unknown whether a real run will print a usage line.

What changed in `scripts/dream.sh`:
• Before the agent runs, the script turns on the audit log (YOYO_AUDIT=1) and notes how many lines .yoyo/audit.jsonl already has (0 if the file doesn't exist).
• Right after the `dream: agent exit= line, a new function report_dream_spend` prints to stderr what this run added to the log:
  • **A usage record appeared:** it prints that record. If there are two (possible with --fallback), it prints both with a count.
  • **No usage record appeared:** it prints `no_terminal_emit`, never zero. This is what a run killed by `timeout` should show, because yoyo doesn't catch that signal and never writes its final record.
  • **Always:** a line with how many records this run added and the file's total size, or a WARNING line if the file is missing.
• The report can't change the script's exit status. Success, failure and timeout all pass through it before the diff-scope check.
• `.yoyo/audit.jsonl is in .gitignore`, so the dream's own commit can't pick it up.

Tests: tests/harness_logic.sh pulls the real function out of dream.sh and runs it against fake audit files in five cases:
• a usage record added this run is printed;
• only tool-call lines → no_terminal_emit;
• usage records only from earlier runs → still no_terminal_emit;
• missing file → the WARNING line;
• two records → both printed.

To check the tests can actually catch a bug, I broke the line-count comparison on purpose. Three checks failed, including both for the earlier-runs case, and the suite went back to 157/157 after I restored the file.

One hiccup: my first edit to dream.sh reported success but never landed; only the call to the function was written. The new test caught it because it couldn't find the function. I re-inserted the block and confirmed it with grep before going on.

Checks run: bash -n scripts/dream.sh, the harness, cargo build, cargo test (no failures), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and cargo fmt --check all pass.

